A||||4||84fieroman||Cooling Fan||||8||
Z||000000||84fieroman||07-17-2001||08:21 AM||||Cooling fan on 84SE does not come on automatically and car overheats.  It will come on when A/C is turned on.  Any ideas of what needs to be replaced to get it to come on automatically??||||reg||8
Z||000001||StuGood||07-17-2001||10:18 AM||||Well, I know little about Dukes, and even less about the 1984 models.  Keeping that in mind...<P>Ordinarily, there's a temp. switch on the engine that grounds a green wire with white stripe, to turn the radiator fan on.  My guess is, that temp. switch needs to be replaced.<P>Alternatively, you can just ground the green/white wire so the fan runs all the time.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||07-17-2001||10:30 AM||||The cooling fan only comes on when the motor is hot enough. That temperature is 235 degrees F! The other way the fan comes on is, as you mentioned, when you turn the A/C "on". Rodney Dickman sells a high temperature switch that will replace you factory unit and turn the fan on when the temperature reaches 195 degrees F and off at 180 degrees F. <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A> <P>Hope this helps,<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||07-17-2001||08:15 PM||||Since it activates with the AC the switch in the block is probably shot.<P>If that's the 2 speed fan. then the both speeds may be out. High activates only around 246F. This fan actually has 3 sets of contacts in the engine.<P>After market switches only replace the 235 contacts. In this case it would at least get low speed working again.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||07-17-2001||09:51 PM||||Get the 210 on and 200 off switch from Rodney. It works great, temp never gets to 220. With this switch you get to use your standard 195 Stat.||||reg||1
